  "notes": "Professional phase only (4 semesters, 63 credits). The Accelerated BSN Option is a 15-month second-bachelor's program for students who already hold a bachelor's degree in another discipline. Prerequisites (completed separately): prior bachelor's degree plus 33 credits of prerequisite coursework per the 2024-2025 catalog (BIO-220/220L, BIO-240/240L, BIO-253/253L, MAT-152, PSY-281, PSY-283, PHI-353, CS-180, plus one 3cr Philosophy distribution course and one 3cr Theology distribution course). NOTE: the 2026-2027 catalog lists 34 prerequisite credits (one credit/course added); itemization of the added requirement was not reachable and is pending re-verification. The four-semester core sequence is unchanged across the 2021-2022, 2024-2025, and 2026-2027 catalogs and matches the current official Barry BSN Accelerated program page (barry.edu, verified 2026-10-01).",
